    "stdout_tail": "4e74-86b1-7fc97c7e2de8\",\n                      \"chunk_id\": \"0edcbfabbe3055b0722ed51c2f1560aafd7c561a6ccb581e28cdeb28161cdd13\",\n                      \"chunk_fingerprint\": \"0edcbfabbe3055b0722ed51c2f1560aafd7c561a6ccb581e28cdeb28161cdd13\",\n                      \"section\": \"YOLOX: Exceeding YOLO Series in 2021 / 1. Introduction\"\n                    },\n                    {\n                      \"quote_text\": \"We have released our code at https://github.com/Megvii-BaseDetection/YOLOX, with ONNX, TensorRT, NCNN and Openvino supported. One more thing worth mentioning, we won the 1st Place on Streaming Perception Challenge (Workshop on Autonomous Driving at CVPR 2021) using a single YOLOX-L model.\\n\\n## 2. YOLOX\\n\\n### 2.1. YOLOX-DarkNet53\\n\\nWe choose YOLOv3 [25] with Darknet53 as our baseline. In the following part, we will walk through the whole system designs in YOLOX step by step.\\n\\n**Implementation details** Our training settings are mostly consistent from the baseline to our final model. We train the models for a total of 300 epochs with 5 epochs warm-up on COCO train2017 [17]. We use stochastic gradient descent (SGD) for training. We use a learning rate of $lr \\\\times BatchSize/64$ (linear scaling \",\n                      \"work_id\": \"52e5de2a-32ef-4e74-86b1-7fc97c7e2de8\",\n                      \"chunk_id\": \"badc0788265df777761ae8248f408fb60dabf6cc7ff3f4b212dcf9340379f324\",\n                      \"chunk_fingerprint\": \"badc0788265df777761ae8248f408fb60dabf6cc7ff3f4b212dcf9340379f324\",\n                      \"section\": \"YOLOX: Exceeding YOLO Series in 2021\"\n                    },\n                    {\n                      \"quote_text\": \"# YOLOX: Exceeding YOLO Series in 2021\\n\\nZheng Ge* Songtao Liu*† Feng Wang Zeming Li Jian Sun \\nMegvii Technology \\n{gezheng, liusongtao, wangfeng02, lizeming, sunjian}@megvii.com\\n\\n![Figure 1: Speed-accuracy trade-off of accurate models (top) and Size-accuracy curve of lite models on mobile devices (bottom) for YOLOX and other state-of-the-art object detectors.](image_url)\\n\\n## Abstract\\n\\nIn this report, we present some experienced improvements to YOLO series, forming a new high-performance detector—YOLOX. We switch the YOLO detector to an anchor-free manner and conduct other advanced detection techniques, i.e., a decoupled head and the leading label assignment strategy SimOTA to achieve state-of-the-art results across a large scale range of models: For YOLO-Nano with only 0.91M parameters and \",\n                      \"work_id\": \"52e5de2a-32ef-4e74-86b1-7fc97c7e2de8\",\n                      \"chunk_id\": \"8962c1fd1ab017a3bc987024585129e708606b2e018f41b93887ee82101eb6fa\",\n                      \"chunk_fingerprint\": \"8962c1fd1ab017a3bc987024585129e708606b2e018f41b93887ee82101eb6fa\",\n                      \"section\": \"YOLOX: Exceeding YOLO Series in 2021\"\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  \"row_count\": 5,\n                  \"truncated\": false\n                }\n              ],\n              \"evidence_origin\": \"parent_tool\",\n              \"confidence\": 0.9,\n              \"terminal_state\": \"succeeded\",\n              \"failure_code\": null\n            }\n          ],\n          \"merge\": {\n            \"evidence_origin\": \"parent_tool\",\n            \"confidence\": 0.9,\n            \"conflict\": null,\n            \"writer_directive\": \"Evidence merge (v3): synthesize a single grounded answer. evidence_origin='parent_tool'. Do not hide tool denials, timeouts, or conflicting VERDICT lines; state them explicitly.\",\n            \"partial_failure\": false\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      \"run_kind\": \"supervisor_specialists_v3\",\n      \"graph_id\": \"supervisor_graph_v3\",\n      \"tool_search_shortlist_ratio_avg\": 0.7143,\n      \"tool_search_deferred_schema_events\": null,\n      \"budget_stop_reasons\": [],\n      \"answer_cla